  "sections": [
    {
      "key": "quickFacts",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/08-carp-like-fishes-2-barbs-minnows-carps-goldfish-etc/scardinius-erythrophthalmus-the-rudd/",
      "html": "<p>The rudd is one of the most common native so-called white fish – and one of the prettiest. The body colouring is silver, often with a touch of brass yellow, and the fins are usually vermilion; the older the fish, the more intense the fin colouring. These are bred fish, intended for aquarium and garden pond keeping, and must not be released into the wild under any circumstances.</p><p>Usually the rudd grows to a length of 15-20 cm, the maximum size is about 50 cm.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "waterConditions",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/08-carp-like-fishes-2-barbs-minnows-carps-goldfish-etc/scardinius-erythrophthalmus-the-rudd/",
      "html": "<p>The species is temperature tolerant and can tolerate water temperatures up to 26°C without damage, so it is very suitable for keeping in aquaria. The aquarium should not be heated, but there is no need to worry if the thermometer shows more than 20°C in midsummer – for some cold water fish already a critical temperature range.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "diet",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/08-carp-like-fishes-2-barbs-minnows-carps-goldfish-etc/scardinius-erythrophthalmus-the-rudd/",
      "html": "<p>The rudd is the native fish with the highest proportion of vegetable food. This is why it is the only native fish species suitable for setting limits to the spread of filamentous algae and duckweed in garden ponds, but you should not expect miracles from it.</p><p>In the aquarium give flake food on a vegetable basis as staple food, plus frozen and live food of all kinds.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "behaviour",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/08-carp-like-fishes-2-barbs-minnows-carps-goldfish-etc/scardinius-erythrophthalmus-the-rudd/",
      "html": "<p>Rudd are schooling fish and very peaceful.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "dimorphism",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/08-carp-like-fishes-2-barbs-minnows-carps-goldfish-etc/scardinius-erythrophthalmus-the-rudd/",
      "html": "<p>Outer sexual characteristics are largely absent; males of the same age are smaller and more delicate than the females.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "reproduction",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/08-carp-like-fishes-2-barbs-minnows-carps-goldfish-etc/scardinius-erythrophthalmus-the-rudd/",
      "html": "<p>They reproduce as egg layers; the spawn is released into finely feathered plants. Rudds do not care for their brood.</p>"
    }
  ],
